            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0699" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10170.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Mexican Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the Mexican Embassy’s
                    note of March 10, 1906,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d567-f1"/> and to subsequent
                    correspondence regarding the extradition of George Deering Reed to Mexico, I
                    have the honor to inform you <pb facs="0700" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/> that the
                    department is in receipt of a telegram, dated the 2d instant, from the Attorney
                    General, in which he says: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Referring to your letter March 13, 1906, and subsequent correspondence, I
                            have the honor to report that George Deering Reed is under arrest and
                            provisional detention in the district of New Jersey, charged with
                            embezzlement in Mexico.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
